description: Julay inter-process communication must use SyncChannel only
globs: src/main/kotlin/julay/**/*.kt
alwaysApply: false
---

# SyncChannel-only IPC

All inter-process communication in Julay must go exclusively through `SyncChannel` (action rendezvous). Do not add shared caches, mutable statics, or other cross-process shortcuts.

- Default and `service` actions → sync size 2
- `internal` actions → sync size 1
- Intentional deadlock → a `service` with no consumers (not a synthetic `deadlock` action)
- Do not reintroduce type-factory interning/caching in `ListType` / `MapType` / `SetType` as an optimization that blurs process isolation assumptions
